From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: docker-mirakc-edcb <docker-mirakc-edcb@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:45:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Reconnect when the stream is closed while receiving

When the server closed the stream or the connection failed, the
receiving thread ended and nothing was received until the next
SetChannel(). EDCB does not tune again by itself, so a restart of
mirakc / Mirakurun lost the rest of every running recording.

Request the stream of the current channel again, after 1, 2, 4 and then
every 5 seconds, until it succeeds or SetChannel() / CloseTuner() stops
the thread. Stopping now shuts the socket down for both directions under
a lock (abort()), which wakes up a blocked recv() or connect() at once;
further connects fail until resume(). The socket is initialized to -1.
